WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.100
This query ranks employees by salary within each
department The function is

00:00:05.125 --> 00:00:10.588
RANK followed by an OVER clause PARTITION BY
department tells PostgreSQL to

00:00:10.612 --> 00:00:15.938
restart the ranking separately for each department
ORDER BY salary descending inside

00:00:15.950 --> 00:00:20.288
the window means the highest salary receives rank
one Because this is

00:00:20.312 --> 00:00:25.162
a window function the individual employee rows
remain in the result We

00:00:25.188 --> 00:00:30.062
are adding a department_rank column rather than
collapsing employees into one department

00:00:30.088 --> 00:00:34.462
row Run the query and watch what happens when the
department changes

00:00:35.338 --> 00:00:39.562
The ranking should start again at one RANK also has
a specific

00:00:39.588 --> 00:00:44.325
behavior with ties If two employees have the same
salary they receive

00:00:44.350 --> 00:00:48.238
the same rank and the next rank can be skipped Later
you

00:00:48.262 --> 00:00:54.288
may also see ROW_NUMBER and DENSE_RANK which handle
ties differently Notice

00:00:54.312 --> 00:00:58.162
that there are two ORDER BY ideas in this query One
is

00:00:58.188 --> 00:01:02.612
inside OVER and defines how the rank is calculated
The final ORDER

00:01:02.638 --> 00:01:07.138
BY controls how the result rows are displayed
Keeping those two purposes

00:01:07.162 --> 00:01:10.012
separate is important when working with window
functions
